REDPATH &amp; FALL, BOSTON,&mdash;Notify all hands that from this time I
      shall talk nothing but selections from my forthcoming book &ldquo;Roughing It.&rdquo;
       Tried it last night. Suits me tip-top.

MY DEAR HOWELLS,&mdash;I am in a sweat and Warner is in another. I told
      Redpath some time ago I would lecture in Boston any two days he might
      choose provided they were consecutive days&mdash;

fields.signature:
Yours truly,
          SAML.  L.  CLEMENS,
          &ldquo;MARK TWAIN,&rdquo;

blocks.text:
DEAR CHARLIE,&mdash;Livy, after reading your letter, used her severest
      form of expression about Mr. Atwater&mdash;to wit: She did not &ldquo;approve&rdquo;
       of his conduct. This made me shudder; for it was equivalent to Allie
      Spaulding's saying &ldquo;Mr. Atwater is a mean thing;&rdquo; or Rev. Thomas Beecher's
      saying &ldquo;Damn that Atwater,&rdquo; or my saying &ldquo;I wish Atwater was three hundred
      million miles in&mdash;&mdash;!&rdquo;

Shan't I write him and say he may call? If you wish to communicate
      directly with him instead, his address is &ldquo;Larchmont Manor, Westchester
      Co., N. Y.&rdquo;

And then if Europe chose to go on stealing from us, we would say with
      noble enthusiasm, &ldquo;American lawmakers do steal but not from foreign
      authors&mdash;Not from foreign authors!&rdquo;
